 "brief_summary": "This trial is conducted globally. The aim of the trial is to examine the dose range, escalation and efficacy of oral semaglutide in subjects with type 2 diabetes.",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* BMI above or equal to 25 and below or equal to 40 kg/m\\^2\n* Subjects diagnosed with T2D (Type 2 diabetes) treated with diet and exercise and/or who have been on a stable dose of metformin for at least 30 days prior to screening\n* HbA1c 7.0-9.5% (53-80 mmol/mol) (both inclusive)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Subjects on selected oral medication with a narrow therapeutic window, such as warfarin, digoxin, tricyclic antidepressants, lithium, aminophylline, theophylline and anticonvulsants\n* History of chronic pancreatitis or idiopathic acute pancreatitis\n* Chronic malabsorption, regardless of aetiology\n* History of Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, or other inflammatory bowel disease\n* Treatment with glucose lowering agent(s) other than metformin as stated in the inclusion criteria in a period of 90 days before the screening visit",
  "sex": "ALL",
  "minimum_age": "18 Years",
  "maximum_age": null,
  "healthy_volunteers": false,
  "std_ages": [
   "ADULT",
   "OLDER_ADULT"
  ]
 },
